package pulseengine:falcon-cascade-step@0.1.0;

/// Sync single-tick facade over the SAME verified cascade pipeline as the P3
/// stream component (`pulseengine:falcon-cascade-stream`), with FLAT scalar args and a
/// scalar return so a CALL-RETURN MC/DC harness (witness) can drive the engine
/// branches.
///
/// Why this exists (#202): the composed stream pipeline's only export is the
/// async-lift `monitor` stream function, which a call-return harness cannot
/// invoke — so witness MC/DC saw 0/2713 branches on it. The `p3` bindgen lifts
/// EVERY export async (`async: all`), so a sync `step` cannot live inside the
/// async stream component; this is a separate SYNC (p2) sibling that runs the
/// identical `cascade_orch` pipeline over the identical verified engines.
///
/// NOT a flight interface: a coverage / tooling entry point. The return is the
/// SUM of the four motor PWMs — a single scalar, so the canonical ABI returns
/// it directly in a register (no return-area pointer the harness would have to
/// synthesise) and the dependency on all four outputs keeps the whole pipeline
/// live against dead-code elimination.
interface step-api {
    step: func(
        ax: f32, ay: f32, az: f32, gx: f32, gy: f32, gz: f32,
        north: f32, east: f32, down: f32, yaw: f32,
    ) -> f32;
}

world cascade-step-component {
    export step-api;
}
